# Heavy, fully re-derivable outputs. The rule this project uses is that
# anything not re-derivable must be committed or hashed; everything ignored
# here is reproducible from `source/` + `params/` + `scripts/` in ~60 s per
# iteration, and the reasoning is written at each line rather than left to be
# guessed at later.

# 52 MB. A byte-identical copy of the operator's Desktop file; its sha256
# (5dfbf1b4...) is recorded in MORNING_REPORT.md and ITERATION_LOG.md, which is
# what makes the copy checkable without storing it twice.
source/

# 289 MB. Regenerated by `iterate.py <NNN> params/iter_<NNN>.json`, which is
# deterministic -- every op is seeded and the identity control proves the engine
# is a no-op at defaults.
blends/

# 389 MB. Same: re-exported from the blend by cull_degenerate.py. The integrity
# gate result for each one is in logs/verify_*.json and cull_*.json, so the
# EVIDENCE about these files is committed even though the files are not.
exports/

# Flat 4-sample mask passes, two per view per iteration, used only to compute
# scalp-visibility percentages. The percentages are in ITERATION_LOG.md.
renders/masks/

# Per-iteration working renders. The ones that carry an argument -- the contact
# sheets and the final candidates -- are NOT ignored and are committed below.
renders/iter*.png
renders/smoke_*.png
renders/orient_*.png
renders/base_*.png
